.TH TPV 1 "October 2026" "version 1.1.0"
.SH NAME
tpv - terminal picture viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tpv
[
.ul
OPTION
]... [
.ul
FILE
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print image file to standard output.
.PP
Supported formats are JPEG, PNG, TGA, BMP, PSD, HDR, PIC
.br
and PNM.
.SH OPTIONS
.BR "-c " DEPTH ", --color-depth=" DEPTH
.RS
Set output color depth. If omitted, highest capability of
.br
the terminal is used.
.PP
Accepted options are:
.br
.BR 24 " - 24-bit/truecolor"
.br
.BR 8 "  - 8-bit/256-color"
.br
.BR 7 "  - 88-color"
.br
.BR 4 "  - 4-bit/16-color"
.br
.BR 3 "  - 3-bit/8-color"
.br
.BR 1 "  - Black and white"
.RE
.PP
.B "-f, --fast"
.RS
Scales by skipping pixels instead of properly scaling down
.br
the image for faster output.
.RE
.PP
.B "-g, --grayscale"
.RS
Print image in grayscale instead of color.
.RE
.PP
.B "-i, --inline"
.RS
Don't clear the screen before printing the image.
.RE
.PP
.B "-n, --no-scaling"
.RS
Print the image at full resolution instead of scaling it
.br
down to fit the terminal. Incompatible with --fast.
.RE
.PP
.B "-p, --progress"
.RS
Show a progress bar while scaling down the image.
.RE
.PP
.B "-v, --no-vert-scaling"
.RS
Scale image to fit as close as possible on width, ignoring
.br
terminal height. Incompatible with --fast.
.RE
.PP
.B "-h, --help"
.RS
Show shortlist of usage and options.
.RE
.SH COMPILING
The program is designed to be compiled using GCC and Make.
.PP
Standard Makefile options of install, uninstall and clean
.br
are available, as well as rebuild for complete recompiling
.br
and debug for making a debuggable version. 
.PP
The following compile options are available when building
.br
from source:
.PP
.RS
.BR nsatinc " - Disable increasing saturation when printing in"
.br
.RS
8/16 color, use the actual pixel color value instead
.RE
.br
.BR truebw " - Check which color is closest to black/white when"
.br
.RS
printing in 8/16 color and use that instead of the
.br
standard BLACK and WHITE
.RE
.br
.BR scaleprec " - Enable more precise scaling for a more correct"
.br
.RS
output but longer processing time
.RE
.br
.BR inline " - Invert usage of the --inline option, so images are"
.br
.RS
printed without clearing the screen by default
.RE
.br
.BR wbsize=n " - Set size of output buffer, default is 16kb"
.RS
.RE
.PP
Further options for image decoding are available and
.br
defined in the header of stb_image.h
.SH BUGS
Bug reports on the projects GitHub
.br
.ul
https://github.com/Dropkickx86/tpv.
.PP
